eturn 0.\n    `n=1`: `a, b = 1, 1`. Return 1.\n    `n=2`: `a, b = 1, 1`, then `a, b = 1, 2`. Return 1.\n    `n=3`: `a, b = 1, 1`, then `a, b = 1, 2`, then `a, b = 2, 3`. Return 2.\n\n    Looks perfect.\n\n    ```python\n    def fib(n):\n        a, b = 0, 1\n        for _ in range(n):\n            a, b = b, a + b\n        return a\n    ```",
